  "quikchat-backend/Dockerfile": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/Dockerfile`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the steps to build a multi-stage Docker image for the QuikChat backend application, resulting in a small, production-ready image.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - This is a Dockerfile and does not contain code definitions.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Multi-stage Build: Uses a `golang:1.21-alpine` image for building and an `alpine:latest` image for the final runtime, reducing image size.\n  - Dependency Caching: Downloads Go modules in a separate step to leverage Docker layer caching.\n  - Static Compilation: `CGO_ENABLED=0` ensures a statically linked binary.\n  - Port Exposure: Exposes port 8080 for the application.\n  - Command: Sets the default command to run the compiled `quikchat` binary.\n",
