  "quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/adapter/storage/postgres/user_repository.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `UserRepository` interface, providing PostgreSQL-specific data access logic for user entities.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `UserRepository`: Implements `repository.UserRepository`, holding a database connection pool.\n      - Fields: `db` (*pgxpool.Pool).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserRepository(db *pgxpool.Pool) *UserRepository`: Public constructor for `UserRepository`.\n    - `Save(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method to insert a new user into the database.\n    - `FindByUsername(ctx context.Context, username string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by their username.\n    - `FindByID(ctx context.Context, id int64) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user by their ID.\n    - `Update(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error`: Public method to update an existing user's profile information.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Repository Pattern: Provides an abstraction layer over database operations.\n  - PostgreSQL Interaction: Uses `pgxpool` for database queries.\n  - Error Handling: Specifically handles `pgx.ErrNoRows` to return `nil` for not found entities.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/friend.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/friend.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the domain models for friend requests and established friendships within the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Constants**:\n    - `FriendRequestStatusPending`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for a pending request.\n    - `FriendRequestStatusAccepted`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for an accepted request.\n    - `FriendRequestStatusDeclined`: `FriendRequestStatus` enum value for a declined request.\n  - **Types**:\n    - `FriendRequestStatus`: String type representing the status of a friend request.\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `FriendRequest`: Represents a request from one user to another.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `SenderID` (int64), `ReceiverID` (int64), `Status` (FriendRequestStatus), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `UpdatedAt` (time.Time).\n    - `Friendship`: Represents an established friendship between two users.\n      - Fields: `UserID1` (int64), `UserID2` (int64), `CreatedAt` (time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Defines core business entities.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/domain/user.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the `User` domain entity structure, representing a user in the QuikChat application.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `User`: Represents a user entity with various attributes.\n      - Fields: `ID` (int64), `Username` (string), `PasswordHash` (string, marked to be ignored in JSON), `DisplayName` (string), `ProfileImageURL` (*string), `CreatedAt` (time.Time), `UpdatedAt` (time.Time), `LastSeenAt` (*time.Time).\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Domain Model: Represents a core business entity.\n  - JSON Tagging: Uses `json:\"...\"` tags for JSON serialization/deserialization, including `json:\"-\"` to hide sensitive fields.\n",
