  "quikchat-backend/internal/service/friend_service.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/service/friend_service.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `FriendUseCase` interface, providing the core business logic for managing friend requests and friendships.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `friendService`: Implements `usecase.FriendUseCase`, holding references to necessary repositories.\n      - Fields: `friendRepo` (repository.FriendRepository), `userRepo` (repository.UserRepository), `blockRepo` (repository.BlockRepository).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewFriendService(friendRepo repository.FriendRepository, userRepo repository.UserRepository, blockRepo repository.BlockRepository) usecase.FriendUseCase`: Public constructor for `friendService`.\n    - `SendRequest(ctx context.Context, senderID int64, receiverUsername string) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`: Public method to send a friend request, including checks for self-request, existing requests, and blocked status.\n    - `RespondToRequest(ctx context.Context, userID, requestID int64, action string) error`: Public method to accept or decline a friend request, with authorization and status checks.\n    - `ListIncomingRequests(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.FriendRequest, error)`: Public method to retrieve all pending friend requests for a specific user.\n    - `ListFriends(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a list of users who are friends with the specified user.\n    - `Unfriend(ctx context.Context, userID int64, friendUsername string) error`: Public method to remove an existing friendship.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Use Case / Service Layer: Encapsulates business rules and orchestrates interactions between repositories.\n  - Dependency Injection: Receives repository interfaces in its constructor.\n  - Business Logic: Contains validation logic for friend requests (e.g., cannot send to self, cannot send to blocked user, cannot send duplicate requests).\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/service/user_service.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/service/user_service.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Implements the `UserUseCase` interface, providing the core business logic for user authentication, profile management, and blocking.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Structs**:\n    - `userService`: Implements `usecase.UserUseCase`, holding references to repositories and JWT configuration.\n      - Fields: `userRepo` (repository.UserRepository), `blockRepo` (repository.BlockRepository), `jwtSecret` (string), `accessTokenExpiry` (time.Duration), `refreshTokenExpiry` (time.Duration).\n  - **Functions**:\n    - `NewUserService(userRepo repository.UserRepository, blockRepo repository.BlockRepository, jwtSecret string, accessExp, refreshExp time.Duration) usecase.UserUseCase`: Public constructor for `userService`.\n    - `Register(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to register a new user, including username uniqueness check and password hashing.\n    - `Login(ctx context.Context, username, password string) (accessToken, refreshToken string, err error)`: Public method to authenticate a user, verifying credentials and generating JWTs.\n    - `GetUserByUsername(ctx context.Context, username string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to retrieve a user's profile by username, clearing the password hash before returning.\n    - `UpdateProfile(ctx context.Context, userID int64, displayName *string, profileImageURL *string) (*domain.User, error)`: Public method to update an authenticated user's display name or profile image URL.\n    - `BlockUser(ctx context.Context, blockerID int64, blockedUsername string) error`: Public method to block another user, including checks for self-blocking and user existence.\n    - `UnblockUser(ctx context.Context, blockerID int64, blockedUsername string) error`: Public method to unblock a user.\n- Notable Patterns or Logic:\n  - Use Case / Service Layer: Encapsulates business rules and orchestrates interactions between repositories.\n  - Dependency Injection: Receives repository interfaces and configuration in its constructor.\n  - Authentication Logic: Handles password hashing (`util.HashPassword`), password verification (`util.CheckPasswordHash`), and JWT generation (`util.GenerateToken`).\n  - Business Rules: Enforces rules like unique usernames, preventing self-blocking, and handling user not found scenarios.\n",
  "quikchat-backend/internal/usecase/friend_usecase.go": "- File Path: `quikchat-backend/internal/usecase/friend_usecase.go`\n- High-Level Purpose: Defines the interface for the business logic (use cases) related to friend management.\n- Definitions in the File:\n  - **Interfaces**:\n    - `FriendUseCase`: Interface for friend-related business operations.\n      - Methods: `SendRequest(ctx context.Context, senderID int64, receiverUsername string) (*domain.FriendRequest, error)`, `RespondToRequest(ctx context.Context, userID, requestID int64, action string) error`, `ListIncomingRequests(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.FriendRequest, error)`, `ListFriends(ctx context.Context, userID int64) ([]*domain.User, error)`, `Unfriend(ctx context.Context, userID int64, friendUsername string) error`.\n",
